---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

/**
 * Grounded in docs/website-recon/RAW-legal.json.
 *
 * Two things NOT in here, on purpose:
 * - No auto-renewal / negative-option billing mechanics. There is no payment
 *   rail and no published price. Describing a renewal flow that doesn't exist
 *   would invent ROSCA and California ARL exposure out of nothing.
 * - Syria is NOT in the sanctions list. E.O. 14312 terminated the emergency and
 *   31 CFR Part 542 was removed from the CFR on 26 August 2025. Every ToS
 *   template on the internet is still wrong about this; copying one would put a
 *   false term in our own contract.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The agreement between iGrowFast LLC and the businesses that use iGrowFast."
  path="/terms"
  updated="16 July 2026"
  summary="The agreement between us and the business using iGrowFast. Written to be read once and understood."
>
  <h2 id="parties">1. Who this is between</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are between <strong>iGrowFast LLC</strong>, a Wyoming limited
    liability company ("iGrowFast", "we"), and the business that uses the service
    ("you"). If you are accepting on behalf of a company, you are confirming you
    have authority to bind it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two documents form part of this agreement and are incorporated by reference:
    our <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a> and our
    <a href="/dpa">Data Processing Addendum</a>. Our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle personal data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="service">2. What we provide</h2>
  <p>
    iGrowFast is software for running cash-on-delivery e-commerce operations:
    orders, carrier integrations, a shared messaging inbox, advertising
    reporting, documents, and reconciliation of what is owed to sellers,
    couriers and media buyers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We track and reconcile. We do not hold, move, or disburse your
    money.</strong> iGrowFast records what is owed and to whom; every actual
    payment happens outside the platform, between you and the person you are
    paying. We are a software provider, not a payment institution, not a bank,
    and not an intermediary in your cash flow.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accounts">3. Accounts and your users</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You are responsible for everything done under your account, and for the accuracy of what you enter.</li>
    <li>You create accounts for your own staff. You decide their roles and what they can see.</li>
    <li>Keep credentials secure. Tell us promptly if you think an account has been compromised.</li>
    <li>You must be able to form a binding contract, and you must not use the service if we have previously terminated you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="yourdata">4. Your data, and your customers' data</h2>
  <p>
    The data you put into iGrowFast is yours. We do not sell it, and we do not
    use it to train anything.
  </p>
  <p>
    Much of that data belongs to <em>your</em> customers — their names, phone
    numbers, addresses, orders and messages. For that data you are the
    controller and we are your processor. That relationship is governed by the
    <a href="/dpa">Data Processing Addendum</a>, and it means:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>You are responsible for having a lawful basis</strong> to hold and use your customers' data.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>You are responsible for consent to message them.</strong> If you
      send marketing or promotional messages, obtaining and recording the
      necessary consent is yours to do, not ours. Messaging platforms enforce
      this, and so do regulators.
    </li>
    <li>You must handle your customers' rights requests. We will support you, and will route to you anyone who contacts us directly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="thirdparty">5. Connecting other services</h2>
  <p>
    You can connect accounts you already hold — couriers, messaging platforms,
    advertising platforms, spreadsheets. When you do:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>You authorise us to access that account on your behalf, for the purpose of providing the service.</li>
    <li>You remain bound by that provider's own terms, and their rules apply to how their data may be used.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Advertising data.</strong> Where staff of yours (for example a
      media buyer) are given access to an advertising account's data, they act as
      your authorised agents, on your authority. You can withdraw it at any time.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Disconnection.</strong> If you tell us to disassociate your account
      from a connected advertising platform, we will do so within
      <strong>three business days</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>We are not responsible for a third-party service changing, breaking, or terminating your access to it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="acceptable">6. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a> is part of this
    agreement. In summary: no unlawful use, no unsolicited messaging, no using
    the service to do to other people what you would not want done to you. We can
    suspend an account that is causing harm, and we will tell you why.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sanctions">7. Sanctions and export control</h2>
  <p>
    iGrowFast LLC is a United States person and must comply with US sanctions
    law wherever it operates. You may not use the service if you are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Located in, ordinarily resident in, or organised under the laws of a
      comprehensively sanctioned region — currently <strong>Cuba, Iran, North
      Korea</strong>, and the <strong>Crimea, Donetsk, Luhansk, Kherson and
      Zaporizhzhia</strong> regions of Ukraine.
    </li>
    <li>
      Listed on, or owned 50% or more by parties listed on, the US Treasury's
      <strong>Specially Designated Nationals (SDN) List</strong> or other
      restricted-party lists.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We reference the SDN List itself rather than reproducing a country list here,
    because sanctions change and a stale list in a contract is a false statement.
    You are responsible for confirming your own eligibility, and you must tell us
    if that changes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fees">8. Fees</h2>
  <p>
    Plans are arranged directly with us. The price, what it covers, and the
    payment terms are whatever we agree with you in writing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="wip">In progress</span> We do not currently operate self-serve
    subscription billing. If and when we do, the terms — price, renewal, and how
    to cancel — will be presented clearly before you are asked for any payment
    details, and this section will be replaced. See
    <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellation</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">9. Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the service running and we take backups. We do not currently
    offer a contractual uptime guarantee, and we would rather say that than print
    a number we have not committed to. Maintenance happens; we will give notice
    where we reasonably can.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ip">10. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The software, design and brand are ours. Your data and your content are
    yours. Nothing here transfers ownership either way. You may not copy, resell,
    reverse-engineer, or white-label the service without our written agreement.
  </p>
  <p>
    Third-party names used on this site — WhatsApp, Google, Shopify,
    WooCommerce, TikTok, Snapchat and others — belong to their owners and are
    used descriptively. We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
    any of them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="warranty">11. Warranties and liability</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided "as is". To the fullest extent the law allows, we
    disclaim implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
    purpose, and non-infringement.
  </p>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law allows, neither party is liable for indirect,
    incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits
    or lost data. Our total liability under this agreement is limited to the fees
    you paid us in the twelve months before the claim arose.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing here excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded — including
    for fraud, or for death or personal injury caused by negligence. If you are
    a consumer, your statutory rights are unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2 id="term">12. Ending it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You may stop using the service and ask us to close your account at any time.</li>
    <li>We may suspend or terminate for material breach, for unlawful use, or if required by law. Except where the breach is serious or urgent, we will tell you and give you a reasonable chance to fix it.</li>
    <li>On termination, we will make your data available for export for a reasonable period, then delete it in line with the <a href="/dpa">DPA</a> and our retention practice.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="law">13. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the <strong>State of Wyoming,
    United States</strong>, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules. The
    courts of Wyoming have jurisdiction. If you are a consumer resident
    elsewhere, this does not deprive you of the protection of mandatory laws in
    your own country.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">14. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we materially change these terms, we will give reasonable notice before
    they take effect. If you don't accept the change, you can stop using the
    service. The date at the top reflects the current version.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">15. Contact</h2>
  <address>
    iGrowFast LLC<br />
    30 N Gould St Ste R<br />
    Sheridan, WY 82801, United States<br />
    <a href="/contact">Contact us</a>
  </address>
</Legal>
